<item><title>Analyst says Nigeria is already a one-man state, not a one-party state</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/analyst-says-nigeria-is-already-a-one-man-state-not-a-one-f17bd9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/analyst-says-nigeria-is-already-a-one-man-state-not-a-one-f17bd9/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>The ruling All Progressives Congress (APC) now controls 31 of Nigeria&apos;s 36 states, up from 21 at the end of the 2023 election cycle.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:06:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" length="32450" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Nigeria&apos;s power minister names gas, grid and metering failures</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-power-minister-names-gas-grid-and-metering-c73fea/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-power-minister-names-gas-grid-and-metering-c73fea/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>Joseph Tegbe told senior editors in Lagos that gas supply, ageing equipment, vandalism and poor metering are holding back the electricity sector.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:02:27 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-power-minister-names-gas-grid-and-metering-c73fea/share.jpg" length="42246" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-s-power-minister-names-gas-grid-and-metering-c73fea/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Nigeria signs $3m deal for 1,000 climate-smart tomato greenhouses in Kano</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-signs-3m-deal-for-1-000-climate-smart-tomato-d12d54/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ng/nigeria-signs-3m-deal-for-1-000-climate-smart-tomato-d12d54/</guid><category>Nigeria</category><description>The deal, signed at COP31 in Türkiye, is funded by the Bank of Agriculture and Turkish firm Direkci Group, which will each put in $1.5 million.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:53:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" length="32450" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ng.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
